Lets the core ask whether a page view shows a frame its browser compositor drew at the view's
size. While the app moves a page's left edge, as the sidebar hides or shows, the core holds each
of the window's CATransaction commits until it does, as Chrome's own windows hold theirs in a live
resize, so the page's right edge and scrollbar never show at the last frame's size (issue #166).
A hook only: the core decides when, and how long to wait.

